1
00:00:03,204 --> 00:00:06,766
Open Commerce, Companies, and open the company.

2
00:00:06,766 --> 00:00:11,674
Northwind Traders already has an admin, Riley, and a buyer, Morgan.

3
00:00:12,127 --> 00:00:14,116
Give a buyer an Order limit.

4
00:00:14,116 --> 00:00:18,737
Morgan may place orders up to three hundred dollars; a bigger order waits

5
00:00:18,737 --> 00:00:21,077
for a company admin to approve it.

6
00:00:21,531 --> 00:00:26,570
Under Payment terms, Net days is how long the company has to pay its invoice.

7
00:00:26,570 --> 00:00:30,456
Deposit is the part paid at checkout, here twenty percent.

8
00:00:30,456 --> 00:00:34,038
Credit limit is the most the company may owe at once:

9
00:00:34,038 --> 00:00:38,106
an order goes on account only as far as the limit allows, and

10
00:00:38,106 --> 00:00:40,231
the rest is paid at checkout.

11
00:00:40,685 --> 00:00:45,555
Monthly budget sends any order that would take the month past it to an admin too.

12
00:00:45,555 --> 00:00:49,585
And Buyers give a purchase order number makes the number required.

13
00:00:50,036 --> 00:00:51,237
Click Save.

14
00:00:51,237 --> 00:00:55,196
The company is saved, and its row shows its terms.

